### Checked other resources

- [x] This is a bug, not a usage question.
- [x] I added a very descriptive title to this issue.
- [x] I searched the LangChain.js documentation with the integrated search.
- [x] I used the GitHub search to find a similar question and didn't find it.
- [x] I am sure that this is a bug in LangChain.js rather than my code.
- [x] The bug is not resolved by updating to the latest stable version of LangChain (`langchain` 1.6.5).

### Example Code

```js
import { FakeListChatModel } from '@langchain/core/utils/testing';
import { Command } from '@langchain/langgraph';
import { createAgent, createMiddleware } from 'langchain';
import { z } from 'zod';

// Inner middleware: records a value in state and asks for the model call to be rerun.
const recordNote = createMiddleware({
  name: 'RecordNote',
  stateSchema: z.object({ note: z.string().optional() }),
  wrapModelCall: async (request, handler) => {
    if (!request.state.note) {
      return new Command({ update: { note: 'recorded' } });
    }

    return handler(request);
  },
});

// Outer middleware: passes the inner result on unchanged.
const passThrough = createMiddleware({
  name: 'PassThrough',
  wrapModelCall: (request, handler) => handler(request),
});

const model = new FakeListChatModel({ responses: ['done'] });

for (const middleware of [[recordNote], [passThrough, recordNote]]) {
  const agent = createAgent({ model, tools: [], middleware });

  try {
    const state = await agent.invoke({ messages: [{ role: 'user', content: 'hi' }] });
    console.log(middleware.map(({ name }) => name).join(' > '), '-> ok, note =', state.note);
  } catch (error) {
    console.log(middleware.map(({ name }) => name).join(' > '), '->', error.name + ':', error.message.split('\n')[0]);
  }
}
```

Output:

```
RecordNote -> ok, note = recorded
PassThrough > RecordNote -> InvalidUpdateError: Invalid update for channel "note" with values ["recorded","recorded"]: LastValue can only receive one value per step.
```

### Error Message and Stack Trace (if applicable)

```
InvalidUpdateError: Invalid update for channel "note" with values ["recorded","recorded"]: LastValue can only receive one value per step.
```

### Description

When a `wrapModelCall` middleware returns a `Command` without calling the handler, and an outer middleware returns that result unchanged, `AgentNode` collects the same `Command` once per middleware layer. The update is then applied once per layer: a `LastValue` channel throws `InvalidUpdateError`, and a reducer channel receives the update several times.

Cause, in `dist/agents/nodes/AgentNode.js`: the validation after each `wrapModelCall` does

```js
else if (isCommand(middlewareResponse)) collectedCommands.push(middlewareResponse);
```

so every layer that returns the same `Command` instance pushes it again. The inner-handler path a few lines above already guards with `!collectedCommands.includes(innerHandlerResult)`; applying the same guard here fixes it:

```js
else if (isCommand(middlewareResponse) && !collectedCommands.includes(middlewareResponse)) collectedCommands.push(middlewareResponse);
```


### System Info

- `langchain` 1.6.5, `@langchain/core` 1.4.0, `@langchain/langgraph` 1.7.3
- Node 24.16.0, macOS (Darwin 25.6.0)
